Thanks Philipp. That is indeed an approach that should work without issue.

In the next version it shouldn't be necessary, but for anyone planning
on excluding regions from the start, Philipp's suggestion is
appropriate.

Chris

On 8/29/19, Philipp Riedel <philipp.rie...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hi Dion,
>
> I'm not sure whether this correctly addresses and helps with your inquiry,
> but I wanted to share an idea.  I needed to exclude regions as well and
> took a different approach which ran without any issues.
>
> First, I excluded the regions from the data.frame that contained the
> regions' time courses (rs-fMRI) and created a correlation matrix from that:
>
>
> roiTC <- subset(roiTC, select = -c(V1, V2, V3, V4, V5, V6, V7))
>
> roiCM <- cor(roiTC)
>
> Second, I customized the atlas I am using:
>
> destrieux.scgm.edit <- destrieux.scgm[order(destrieux.scgm$index),]
>
> destrieux.scgm.edit <- destrieux.scgm.edit[-c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6), ]
>
> atlas <- 'destrieux.scgm.edit'
>
> Best,
> Philipp
>
>
